IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pip-nouns`

-- Schedule 1, Part 2: the daily living activities table.
--
-- The table is DATA: one row for each descriptor, with the activity (column 1),
-- the words of the descriptor (column 2) and its points (column 3), copied from the
-- table lines of the text by a script that is not kept in this folder. Whether a descriptor is satisfied is a
-- finding of fact; regulation 7 (pip-part2-assessment.l4) says which descriptor
-- applies to C, and regulation 5 (same module) adds the points.
--
-- A descriptor with limbs, such as 2b "Needs -(i) ...; or (ii) ...; or (iii) ...", is
-- one row: the limbs are alternatives inside the words of the descriptor.
--
-- The rows are named for the descriptor (for example `row for daily living 3b`).
-- Each activity has a function from the descriptors of that activity to its row; its
-- last constructor, "no descriptor ... applies", is the explicit not-covered case that
-- regulation 7 can reach, and has no row.

§ `Schedule 1, Part 2: the daily living activities table`

§§ `Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 1: Preparing food`

-- Row of the table: activity, letter, points, words
-- src:567 | | 1. Preparing food. | a. Can prepare and cook a simple meal unaided. | 0 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 1, descriptor a (src:567)
`row for daily living 1a` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 1, preparing food`, `letter a`, 0, "Can prepare and cook a simple meal unaided."

-- src:568 | | b. Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal. | 2 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 1, descriptor b (src:568)
`row for daily living 1b` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 1, preparing food`, `letter b`, 2, "Needs to use an aid or appliance to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal."

-- src:569 | | c. Cannot cook a simple meal using a conventional cooker but is able to do so using a microwave. | 2 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 1, descriptor c (src:569)
`row for daily living 1c` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 1, preparing food`, `letter c`, 2, "Cannot cook a simple meal using a conventional cooker but is able to do so using a microwave."

-- src:570 | | d. Needs prompting to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal. | 2 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 1, descriptor d (src:570)
`row for daily living 1d` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 1, preparing food`, `letter d`, 2, "Needs prompting to be able to either prepare or cook a simple meal."

-- src:571 | | e. Needs supervision or assistance to either prepare or cook a simple meal. | 4 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 1, descriptor e (src:571)
`row for daily living 1e` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 1, preparing food`, `letter e`, 4, "Needs supervision or assistance to either prepare or cook a simple meal."

-- src:572 | | f. Cannot prepare and cook food. | 8 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 1, descriptor f (src:572)
`row for daily living 1f` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 1, preparing food`, `letter f`, 8, "Cannot prepare and cook food."

GIVEN d IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 1`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 1` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `daily living 1a` THEN JUST `row for daily living 1a`
    WHEN `daily living 1b` THEN JUST `row for daily living 1b`
    WHEN `daily living 1c` THEN JUST `row for daily living 1c`
    WHEN `daily living 1d` THEN JUST `row for daily living 1d`
    WHEN `daily living 1e` THEN JUST `row for daily living 1e`
    WHEN `daily living 1f` THEN JUST `row for daily living 1f`
    WHEN `no descriptor of daily living activity 1 applies` THEN NOTHING

