-- src:620 | | c. Needs prompting or assistance to be able to make simple budgeting decisions. | 4 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 10, descriptor c (src:620)
`row for daily living 10c` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions`, `letter c`, 4, "Needs prompting or assistance to be able to make simple budgeting decisions."

-- src:621 | | d. Cannot make any budgeting decisions at all. | 6 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 2, activity 10, descriptor d (src:621)
`row for daily living 10d` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions`, `letter d`, 6, "Cannot make any budgeting decisions at all."

GIVEN d IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 10`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 10` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `daily living 10a` THEN JUST `row for daily living 10a`
    WHEN `daily living 10b` THEN JUST `row for daily living 10b`
    WHEN `daily living 10c` THEN JUST `row for daily living 10c`
    WHEN `daily living 10d` THEN JUST `row for daily living 10d`
    WHEN `no descriptor of daily living activity 10 applies` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 1, Part 2: all the rows, in the order of the table`

GIVETH A LIST OF `a row of Schedule 1`
`all the rows of the daily living activities table` MEANS
